Positive Behavioral Change: By utilizing a targeted pelvic floor relaxation breathing technique (diaphragmatic breathing) during pain spikes, you will actively decrease the muscular clamping around your pelvic organs, directly reducing the nerve compression and rewarding yourself with a lower perception of pain.
